🔹 Step 9 — Average 3 Replicates per Ligand
After you have the same files (RMSD_backbone_lig.xvg, etc.) for Run 1–3, use this to average:
awk '/^[^#@]/{print $1, $2}' run1/Analysis/RMSD_backbone_lig.xvg > tmp1.dat
awk '/^[^#@]/{print $2}' run2/Analysis/RMSD_backbone_lig.xvg > tmp2.dat
awk '/^[^#@]/{print $2}' run3/Analysis/RMSD_backbone_lig.xvg > tmp3.dat

paste tmp1.dat tmp2.dat tmp3.dat | \
awk '{t=$1; mean=($2+$3+$4)/3; sd=sqrt((($2-mean)^2+($3-mean)^2+($4-mean)^2)/3); print t, mean, sd}' \
> Analysis/RMSD_backbone_lig_avg.dat
Then plot mean ± SD → gives Figure 1 (average RMSD).
You can later do the same for ligand RMSD, H-bonds, or SASA if you want averaged curves.
________________________________________
🔹 Step 10 — Comparing Ligands (Final Figures)
Once you finish all 3 runs for all 4 ligands + apo:
•	Each ligand’s mean RMSD ± SD → plot together (Figure 1).
•	Ligand RMSDs → Figure 2.
•	RMSF (apo vs holo) → Figure 3.
•	H-bond count vs time → Figure 4.
•	SASA (polar/nonpolar/backbone) → Figure 5.
Each of these directly matches the analyses above.
